@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+## Context
+
+`price` parses both ends as midnight UTC and multiplies by the daily price. Bookings store epoch-millisecond ranges, so overlap checks already work for any instants.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- A period is hourly when `end - start` is under 24 hours and not both ends are at midnight (which cannot be under a day anyway). Both ends must be on the hour UTC (minutes, seconds, ms all zero); otherwise rejected. Anything else follows the existing whole-day rules.
+- Hourly total = `hourlyPrice × hours`, no discount. Assumption: the long-stay discount only applies from 3 days, so it never concerns hourly rentals.
+- A period of exactly 24 hours not starting at midnight is not "shorter than a day" and is rejected.
+- Hourly periods may cross midnight.
+- `hourlyPrice` is optional; when present it must be a non-negative integer, like `dailyPrice`.
+- `availability` is unchanged (whole-day queries), but it already excludes items with overlapping hourly bookings.
+
+## Risks
+
+- Hourly bookings of a day-priced item are blocked by design; the desk must register an `hourlyPrice` to enable them.
